From: ansuz-port (Nord2 Metal port ledger)
Subject: [PATCH 0099] nord2: core-aware placement on the big cores, per-CPU clock report (opt-in)

Ported from rotten-apple (ansuz-metal) xnu 0212/0236 (core-aware placement for
the SMP clutch scheduler) and 0095/0140 (CPU clock by dependent-add chain).
Default behaviour unchanged (n2sch=0); per-switch accounting + NORD2 SCHED /
NORD2 CPUCLK log lines on. Boot-args: n2sch n2schpri n2big n2schst n2schab
n2clk n2csram (see osfmk/kern/nord2_sched.c). Applies after 0084.
Link levels: (a) measurement only = add nord2_sched.o + nord2_sched_sysctl.o;
(b) placement = also replace archive members sched_clutch.o + sched_prim.o.
